---
import { Picture } from "astro:assets";
import { profile } from "../data/site";
import portrait from "../assets/portrait.png";
---

<section class="section about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
  <div class="wrap about__wrap">
    <figure class="about__photo" data-reveal data-cursor="nerd">
      <Picture src={portrait} formats={["avif", "webp"]} widths={[288, 460]} sizes="min(24rem, 100vw)" alt={`Portrait of ${profile.name}`} />
    </figure>
    <div class="about__text">
      <h2 class="stretch about__title" id="about-title" data-stretch><span>Hi, I'm</span> <span>Sri Harsh</span></h2>
      <div class="about__body">
        <p data-reveal style="--i:0">
          I’m a full-stack developer in Enschede. I grew up in New Delhi, came to the Netherlands in 2019 to study
          Computer Science at the University of Twente, and now work at Just Eat Takeaway.com on the pages people
          use to follow their order.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal style="--i:1">
          I like working close to the people who use what I build. At AppsForTableau that meant joining customer
          calls, then going back and rebuilding the part they had struggled with. Now it means watching real-user
          data after a release, because a feature isn’t done until it’s clearly better.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal style="--i:2">
          Most of my curiosity right now goes into AI as part of how software gets made. The reporting tools I built
          at work started as an experiment and now help us catch production incidents. With AI taking the repetitive
          parts, one developer can cover far more ground, from the first sketch to the production alert.
        </p>
        <p data-reveal style="--i:3">
          Outside work, I build small things for myself: years of location history on a night map, a year of
          takeaway orders read back as a story. They’re where I try ideas before I’d defend them at work.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="about__cta" data-reveal style="--i:4">
        <a class="btn" href="/cv/">Read the full CV</a>
        <a class="btn btn--ghost" href="#contact">Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about__wrap {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .about__wrap {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) 1.4fr;
      align-items: start;
    }
  }
  .about__photo {
    position: relative;
    max-width: 24rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-l);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: var(--marigold);
    rotate: -3deg;
    box-shadow: 0 30px 60px -30px rgb(var(--shadow) / 0.5);
    transition: rotate 700ms var(--ease-out), transform 700ms var(--ease-out);
  }
  @media (hover: hover) and (pointer: fine) {
    .about__photo:hover {
      rotate: 0deg;
      transform: scale(1.02);
    }
  }
  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .about__photo {
      position: sticky;
      top: 7rem;
    }
  }
  .about__photo img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    /* The cutout sits slightly low on the marigold card, like a passport photo. */
    translate: 0 4%;
    scale: 1.04;
  }
  /* Size the heading to its own column, so "Sri Harsh" fits at full stretch. */
  .about__text {
    container-type: inline-size;
  }
  .about__title {
    font-size: min(6.5rem, 12.5cqi);
  }
  .about__title span {
    display: inline-block;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .about__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.2rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    max-width: 38rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.4vw, 1.3rem);
  }
  .about__cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 2.25rem;
  }
</style>
